	<description>HER PERFECT LIFE IS A PERFECT LIE.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;As a teenager at the prestigious Bradley School, Ani FaNelli endured a shocking, public humiliation that left her desperate to reinvent herself. Now, with a glamorous job, expensive wardrobe, and handsome blue blood fiancé, she’s this close to living the perfect life she’s worked so hard to achieve.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;But Ani has a secret.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;There’s something else buried in her past that still haunts her, something private and painful that threatens to bubble to the surface and destroy everything.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;With a singular voice and twists you won’t see coming, Luckiest Girl Alive explores the unbearable pressure that so many women feel to “have it all” and introduces a heroine whose sharp edges and cutthroat ambition have been protecting a scandalous truth, and a heart that's bigger than it first appears.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;The question remains: will breaking her silence destroy all that she has worked for—or, will it at long last, set Ani free?</description>
